tag example;

extern save(value: *int@immortal): int;

main(): int {
    save(new int[1](1))
}

/* expect compile {|
noregion_retaining_argument.l8:6:10

    save(new int[1](1))
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^

main passes this allocation to parameter value of save, whose @immortal
contract allows it to retain the value after the call. Memory allocated
inside a region is freed when that region ends.

If this value should be retained, declare main as noregion. Its callers
also need noregion. This prevents those functions from being called
inside a region.

If the value is only needed during the call, use a parameter contract
that permits borrowing it for the call. Only change a callee's @immortal
contract if its implementation does not retain the value.

|} */
